how to go  safe mode
-------------------------------
Windows + R > msconfig > enter > boot tab > minimal > apply >ok >  restart

How to exit Safe Mode
-------------------------------
Windows + R > msconfig > enter > boot tab uncheck > apply >  ok > restart

how to go startup setting 
--------------------------------------
(if pc is black screen how to go startup option )
Ctrl + Alt + Delete → Power icon → hold Shift → Restart

(If the Windows 10 screen is completely black, you can still enter Safe Mode using the Windows Recovery Environment)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Best method: Force Windows Recovery
Turn off the PC completely
Hold the Power button for about 10 seconds.
Turn the PC ON.
As soon as you see the Windows logo or spinning dots, hold the Power button again to turn it off.
Repeat this 2–3 times.
On the next startup, Windows should show:
Preparing Automatic Repair → Diagnosing your PC
Choose:
Advanced options → Troubleshoot → Advanced options → Startup Settings → Restart
After restart, press:
4 = Safe Mode
5 = Safe Mode with Networking
